---
const circles = [
  {
    title: 'Systems',
    className: 'systems',
    capabilities: ['flow boundaries', 'sequence logic', 'state contracts'],
  },
  {
    title: 'Human Behavior',
    className: 'behavior',
    capabilities: ['trust under pressure', 'workarounds', 'decision delay'],
  },
  {
    title: 'Language / Interpretation',
    className: 'language',
    capabilities: ['implicit assumptions', 'instruction load', 'meaning gaps'],
  },
];
---

<section id="venn" class="section-focus">
  <div class="container split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Why this reads differently</p>
      <h2>Guidance failure sits between system logic, human behavior, and interpretation.</h2>
      <p class="section-copy">Most teams diagnose the surface: copy, friction, tickets, edge cases. The review reads the crossing point where the product stopped making the next action understandable enough to take.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="venn-panel" aria-label="Guidance Failure Architecture Venn diagram">
      <div class="venn-center">Guidance Failure Architecture</div>
      {circles.map((circle) => (
        <button class={`venn-circle ${circle.className}`} type="button">
          <span>{circle.title}</span>
          <ul>
            {circle.capabilities.map((capability) => <li>{capability}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
